NetRocket
=========

This project is a ground-up reimplementation of the ideas in:

  OpenNetLimit — https://github.com/SysAdminDoc/OpenNetLimit
  Copyright (c) the OpenNetLimit contributors
  Licence: MIT
  Analysed at commit f26b46cc93887fab6bbeed2091b5d365fa516e2b

No source code from OpenNetLimit is included. The analysis that informed the
design, including the file:line evidence for every behavioural difference, is
in docs/REVERSE-ENGINEERING.md.

The reverse-engineering methodology (evidence tagging, provenance, fail-closed
unknowns) comes from:

  REA — https://github.com/morluto/rea
  Licence: see the upstream repository

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WinDivert (NOT bundled)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

NetRocket links dynamically against WinDivert 2.2:

  WinDivert — https://github.com/basil00/WinDivert
  Copyright (c) Basil (basil00)
  Licence: dual LGPLv3 / GPLv2

No WinDivert source or binary is distributed in this repository. If you ship
the driver (WinDivert.dll, WinDivert64.sys) alongside these binaries you must:

  * include WinDivert's licence text,
  * state that the driver is a separate, replaceable component (LGPL relinking),
  * leave the driver files unmodified.

See docs/SECURITY.md, "WinDivert licensing and distribution".

